\begin{align*}  
x&\equiv 4 \bmod 11\\
x&\equiv 1 \bmod 7.
\end{align*} 
Taking all possible values of $x$ modulo $77$ : 
\begin{align*}  
x&\equiv 4 \bmod 11\\
x&\equiv 1 \bmod 7 \\
&\equiv 45 \bmod 77\\
&\equiv 45+77k, k\in\mathbb{Z}. 
\end{align*} 
